{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"agent_message","text":"The key-based selector is both exact and about 10% faster, and in-place sigmoid gives a small additional gain. I’m making one final mixed-precision check: disabling reduced-precision BF16 reductions may make PyTorch’s direct BF16-input/FP32-output GEMM adopt the reference accumulation path, which would remove both casts if it matches bitwise."}}
