{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_92","type":"agent_message","text":"Row chunking either changes rocBLAS’s accumulation bits or loses time to extra launches, so I’ve rejected it. The current version keeps the exact single GEMM, uses in-place sigmoid, and uses stable sortable keys for both routing top-k stages; I’m verifying that refined version across all 16 workloads now."}}
